cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this cookbook, please cite it as below."
authors:
  # add additional entries for each author -- see https://github.com/citation-file-format/citation-file-format/blob/main/schema-guide.md
  - family-names: Panta
    given-names: Aashish
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0009-0001-5843-2098
    affiliation: Scientific Computing and Imaging Institute, University of Utah
  - name: "NSDF-OpenVISUS cookbook contributors"
    website: "https://github.com/sci-visus/openvisuspy/graphs/contributors"
title: "NSDF-OpenVISUS Cookbook"
abstract: "NSDF-OpenVISUS Cookbook provides practical, reproducible notebooks for accessing, subsetting, and visualizing large-scale scientific datasets using OpenVISUS and Pelican-based cloud data delivery. The materials demonstrate multiresolution data queries, region- and depth-specific exploration workflows, and publication-ready visualization patterns for ocean and atmosphere use cases, enabling researchers to quickly adapt the examples to their own data-intensive science applications."
